me team  at one point montreal plays ottawa four  straight despite that the new  configuration does mean  extra strain for the canadian teams  we're in the division that travels the  most  of all the divisions in this league this  year we're going from one end of the  country  to the other the nfl wrapped up its  regular season sunday  there were hiccups but they did get  through without any cancellations  that bodes well for the nhl every sport  is taking best practices from the other  sports  and it's good to see that the  commissioners are all talking to each  other sharing that intel  now ratings were weak for last year's  nhl playoffs playoff hockey in august  was perhaps not a natural sell  the hope is if this season wraps up as  scheduled next season could start at the  normal time of the year the fall  possibly post pandemic hopefully  mike armstrong global news montreal  and that is global national for this  monday night i'm robin gill  tonight your canada is the yukon river  in whitehorse  we love seeing your part of the country  so email your photos to viewers at  globalnational.com  thank you for watching and i'll see you  back here tomorrow have a great night  [Music]  you
 

